        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues on the clickable header `<div>` in `collapsible.tsx` (line 122). I couldn't re-run the linter: there's no `node_modules` in the folder and running `npx` needed approval, so the fix hasn't been checked by the linter.\n\nWhat I changed on that one element:\n- **`role=\"button\"`** fixes `no-static-element-interactions`, following the rule's help text (\"Add a role attribute\").\n- **An `onKeyDown` handler** fixes `click-events-have-key-events`. Enter or Space calls `openTrigger()`, the same as a click. It also blocks the default action, so Space doesn't scroll the page.\n- **`tabIndex={0}`** lets keyboard users tab to the header. Without it, the key handler could never fire, and `interactive-supports-focus` would likely flag it next.\n- **`aria-expanded={open}`** tells screen readers whether the section is open.\n\nClicks, layout and styles are unchanged.\n\nI kept the `<div>` and didn't switch to a real `<button>`. The `label` passed in is an `<h3>`, and a heading inside a `<button>` is invalid HTML. A `<button>` would also bring default browser styles (border, background, font, width) that change how the header looks.\n\nIf your Ultracite setup turns on `jsx-a11y/prefer-tag-over-role`, it would flag `role=\"button\"`. Clearing that would mean moving the button inside the `<h3>` (the standard accordion pattern), which changes how `label` is passed in, so that's your call.",
